(7291275, 1136266, 113156, '<td valign="top">Didn''t vote, didn''t comment, stupid me. You made the mundane into a satisfying unfinished tale, brilliant light, excellent photo.</td>', 'Didn''t vote, didn''t comment, stupid me. You made the mundane into a satisfying unfinished tale, brilliant light, excellent photo.', '2014-12-08 11:39:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291276, 1135437, 113156, '<td valign="top">This took a while but when it hits it great.</td>', 'This took a while but when it hits it great.', '2014-12-08 11:40:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291279, 1136266, 16148, '<td valign="top">Don, this is brilliant stuff!  Pure seeing and genuine photography.  Love the subtle tilt, noise, slightly off center composition, and hints of detail in the dark negative space.  Thanks for retaining the look and feel of an actual photograph.</td>', 'Don, this is brilliant stuff!  Pure seeing and genuine photography.  Love the subtle tilt, noise, slightly off center composition, and hints of detail in the dark negative space.  Thanks for retaining the look and feel of an actual photograph.', '2014-12-08 12:10:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291302, 1136215, 112739, '<td valign="top">Nice scene Alex. should have scored higher IMO.</td>', 'Nice scene Alex. should have scored higher IMO.', '2014-12-08 13:18:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291310, 1136189, 112739, '<td valign="top">Thanks for not cropping the upper bird out. It wouldn''t work as well without it. Makes for a strong triangle composition.</td>', 'Thanks for not cropping the upper bird out. It wouldn''t work as well without it. Makes for a strong triangle composition.', '2014-12-08 13:29:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291313, 1136432, 112739, '<td valign="top">Really great shot Tom! Happy Holidays.</td>', 'Really great shot Tom! Happy Holidays.', '2014-12-08 13:34:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291315, 1136217, 112739, '<td valign="top">The little <a href="//world.honda.com/ASIMO/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Honda robot</a> would make this the complete image. Very cool image Doc.</td>', 'The little Honda robot would make this the complete image. Very cool image Doc.', '2014-12-08 13:37:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291323, 1136412, 108040, '<td valign="top">Congratulations and til hamingju.</td>', 'Congratulations and til hamingju.', '2014-12-08 13:58:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291329, 1136344, 60173, '<td valign="top">What really gets me are the marks on the collar where it has been let out as the pup on the right grew. I doubt these are the same breed, but you captured what seems to be a moment between an adult dog and a younger dog. The adult dog even seems to have some grey fur on his snout. I wonder what wisdom the older dog was passing to the pup.</td>', 'What really gets me are the marks on the collar where it has been let out as the pup on the right grew. I doubt these are the same breed, but you captured what seems to be a moment between an adult dog and a younger dog. The adult dog even seems to have some grey fur on his snout. I wonder what wisdom the older dog was passing to the pup.', '2014-12-08 14:07:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291343, 1135340, 123833, '<td valign="top">The composition does not quite work for me. The building distracts and the drama of the water is not sufficiently emphasized. The colors look a bit too green. It is also a common problem that you know the context of the location well and see more in the photo than a casual observer.<br/> <br/>Disclaimer - this is a reply to your request for more feedback and meant to be an attempt to understand the DPC score.</td>', 'The composition does not quite work for me. The building distracts and the drama of the water is not sufficiently emphasized. The colors look a bit too green. It is also a common problem that you know the context of the location well and see more in the photo than a casual observer. Disclaimer - this is a reply to your request for more feedback and meant to be an attempt to understand the DPC score.', '2014-12-08 14:28:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291353, 1136481, 20799, '<td valign="top">Spotted you too, there are animals hidden in there. Who else.</td>', 'Spotted you too, there are animals hidden in there. Who else.', '2014-12-08 14:34:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291355, 1136346, 30214, '<td valign="top">the boy and his shadow, cordoned by the two watchful adults... awesome composition John<br/>1 I did not know you switched to Sony, how does it compare to Fuji?</td>', 'the boy and his shadow, cordoned by the two watchful adults... awesome composition John1 I did not know you switched to Sony, how does it compare to Fuji?', '2014-12-08 14:35:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291367, 1135340, 170281, '<td valign="top">I agree with some of the other comments.  It does look a bit flat and out of focus, especially the rock outcrop on the right and cloud definition, perhaps due to the heavy mist.  The colors of the foliage in the background do not stand out.  Could the topaz denoise had an effect on that?  I do like the framing and subject matter.</td>', 'I agree with some of the other comments.  It does look a bit flat and out of focus, especially the rock outcrop on the right and cloud definition, perhaps due to the heavy mist.  The colors of the foliage in the background do not stand out.  Could the topaz denoise had an effect on that?  I do like the framing and subject matter.', '2014-12-08 15:11:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291378, 1136266, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bvy:</b></div><hr/><i>(As for the tilt, it''s no more tilted than my head might be if I were standing in front of it. So why mention it?) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>DPC COMPELS ME!!!</td>', 'Originally posted by bvy:(As for the tilt, it''s no more tilted than my head might be if I were standing in front of it. So why mention it?)   DPC COMPELS ME!!!', '2014-12-08 16:05:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291394, 1136392, 16148, '<td valign="top">I was coming back to look through a few images from the November Free Study and noticed something unusual.  In your voting breakdown you have a double peak.  More 5''s and 7''s than 6''s.  I don''t remember seeing this before, have no idea what it means, but find it fascinating.   Score isn''t everything but voting patterns are interesting.</td>', 'I was coming back to look through a few images from the November Free Study and noticed something unusual.  In your voting breakdown you have a double peak.  More 5''s and 7''s than 6''s.  I don''t remember seeing this before, have no idea what it means, but find it fascinating.   Score isn''t everything but voting patterns are interesting.', '2014-12-08 17:08:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291396, 1135143, 30214, '<td valign="top">An iconic composition of Jesus, Peter and Paul in a nightmarish dream. Fantastic catch!</td>', 'An iconic composition of Jesus, Peter and Paul in a nightmarish dream. Fantastic catch!', '2014-12-08 17:20:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291401, 1136344, 68504, '<td valign="top">really like this. a true meeting of minds.</td>', 'really like this. a true meeting of minds.', '2014-12-08 18:11:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291403, 1135143, 68504, '<td valign="top">we will have shivers for days... and you must have been close, with your tiny xz1. the Durer effect only adds to the frisson.</td>', 'we will have shivers for days... and you must have been close, with your tiny xz1. the Durer effect only adds to the frisson.', '2014-12-08 18:17:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291423, 1135340, 3724, '<td valign="top">When viewing this, a scene which has billions of images made of it, I noticed that the colour &amp; contrast invokes a successfully flat &amp; nostalgic 2D post card quality - <br/>appropriate for the image, as I see that sentiment.<br/>The colour work is very good, but the sharpen and contrast is too strong. Voted 7</td>', 'When viewing this, a scene which has billions of images made of it, I noticed that the colour & contrast invokes a successfully flat & nostalgic 2D post card quality - appropriate for the image, as I see that sentiment.The colour work is very good, but the sharpen and contrast is too strong. Voted 7', '2014-12-08 20:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291424, 1136321, 83149, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Maharet:</b></div><hr/><i> I think this is beautiful but noise is just a little bit too much. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I added the grain in post to give an ''aged'' look to the photo.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2014-12-08 20:03:23.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Maharet: I think this is beautiful but noise is just a little bit too much.   I added the grain in post to give an ''aged'' look to the photo.', '2014-12-08 20:02:01.000000', '2014-12-08 20:03:23.000000', 0),
(7291446, 1135340, 30364, '<td valign="top">I scored it 4 . Not for any of the mild quibbles raised about composition or focus, etc. but because it is simply a boring picture.   So for me, the only way to make the photograph better is to not take it at all.<br/> <br/>That''s harsh, if your intention with this picture is solely to practice the technical aspects of photography.  But even if your intent was limited to that, why point the camera at something of which there are already fifty thousand photos taken every hour?  Especially from the same angle, at the same time, and same point of view?  It''s going to be a cliche and boring, no matter who takes the picture and with what.<br/> <br/>I can anticipate that you (and many others) would resent my feedback, and say ''''But I''m just trying to learn to be a better photographer''.  But the point of owning a camera is <i>not</i> to be a photographer, it''s to take pictures.  And if the pictures are standard views of standard subjects, they simply can''t be interesting.  And if a picture isn''t interesting, nothing else matters.<br/> <br/>Of course I''m not much of a photographer, by popular acclaim.. But it wasn''t what was popular you asked about, it was what (about your picture) was unpopular.  And that''s my view. <br/> <br/>If it''s any consolation, some of the most popular and successful photographers at DPC seem to take nothing but boring pictures, presumably having become afraid to do anything different.<br/> <br/>Don''t do that.  Let curiosity be your guide.</td>', 'I scored it 4 . Not for any of the mild quibbles raised about composition or focus, etc. but because it is simply a boring picture.   So for me, the only way to make the photograph better is to not take it at all. That''s harsh, if your intention with this picture is solely to practice the technical aspects of photography.  But even if your intent was limited to that, why point the camera at something of which there are already fifty thousand photos taken every hour?  Especially from the same angle, at the same time, and same point of view?  It''s going to be a cliche and boring, no matter who takes the picture and with what. I can anticipate that you (and many others) would resent my feedback, and say ''''But I''m just trying to learn to be a better photographer''.  But the point of owning a camera is not to be a photographer, it''s to take pictures.  And if the pictures are standard views of standard subjects, they simply can''t be interesting.  And if a picture isn''t interesting, nothing else matters. Of course I''m not much of a photographer, by popular acclaim.. But it wasn''t what was popular you asked about, it was what (about your picture) was unpopular.  And that''s my view.  If it''s any consolation, some of the most popular and successful photographers at DPC seem to take nothing but boring pictures, presumably having become afraid to do anything different. Don''t do that.  Let curiosity be your guide.', '2014-12-08 20:58:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291471, 1136251, 8759, '<td valign="top">Excellent, Lev!</td>', 'Excellent, Lev!', '2014-12-08 21:48:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291487, 1136203, 112739, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> Bird in captivity.  How hard is it to poke a camera lens into the face of a zoo bird? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Everyone has a right to shoot what they please and enter it, no matter how hard it was to take the photo. <br/>I remember when I started taking photos, and I went to the zoo one day to take pics of animals. Not very many of the pics were keepers even though I took over 400 shots in one day. Point is, doesn''t matter how hard it was, what matters is what the photo says to the viewer. Congrats on HM in a FS.</td>', 'Originally posted by hahn23: Bird in captivity.  How hard is it to poke a camera lens into the face of a zoo bird?   Everyone has a right to shoot what they please and enter it, no matter how hard it was to take the photo. I remember when I started taking photos, and I went to the zoo one day to take pics of animals. Not very many of the pics were keepers even though I took over 400 shots in one day. Point is, doesn''t matter how hard it was, what matters is what the photo says to the viewer. Congrats on HM in a FS.', '2014-12-08 22:13:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291491, 1136329, 123833, '<td valign="top">This is a great lens so it can''t be it! ;)<br/> <br/>I think a shorter exposure, say 0.5s, could make the figures more visible while still interestingly blurred :)</td>', 'This is a great lens so it can''t be it! ;) I think a shorter exposure, say 0.5s, could make the figures more visible while still interestingly blurred :)', '2014-12-08 22:20:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291494, 1136352, 50641, '<td valign="top">oh I really liked this when i was flipping through</td>', 'oh I really liked this when i was flipping through', '2014-12-08 22:29:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291517, 1135581, 100831, '<td valign="top">Cool calm and collected..</td>', 'Cool calm and collected..', '2014-12-08 23:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7291532, 1135340, 123833, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ubique:</b></div><hr/><i> (and many others) would resent my feedback </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, I mostly resent it. It goes against the friendly competitive spirit of DPC and hurts the most enthusiastic photographers unnecessarily. I see your feedback as a BIG ego trip.</td>', 'Originally posted by ubique: (and many others) would resent my feedback  Yes, I mostly resent it. It goes against the friendly competitive spirit of DPC and hurts the most enthusiastic photographers unnecessarily. I see your feedback as a BIG ego trip.', '2014-12-09 01:04:01.000000', NULL, 0),
